{"id":"e02t3","name":"Longest Stockout Streak","lang":"sql","entry":null,"params":[],"limit_s":10,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>The supply team wants to find the products that stayed out of stock for the longest time.</p>\n<p>You have the table <b>daily_stock</b>. It has the following columns:</p>\n<ul><li><code>sku</code> - the product code;</li><li><code>day</code> - the date of the stock count (date);</li><li><code>qty</code> - the stock at the end of the day (integer). It is null when the count failed.</li></ul>\n<p>There is at most one row per <code>sku</code> and <code>day</code>. Some days are missing.</p>\n<p>A <b>stockout day</b> is a row with <code>qty = 0</code>. A <b>stockout streak</b> is a group of stockout days of the same SKU on <b>consecutive calendar days</b>. A missing day, a day with a null quantity, or a day with a positive quantity ends the streak.</p>\n<p>Your task is to return, for each SKU that has at least one stockout day, its longest streak with <code>sku</code>, <code>streak_start</code>, <code>streak_end</code> and <code>days</code> (the number of days of the streak). If a SKU has several streaks of the same length, return the earliest one. Sort by <code>days</code> descending, then <code>sku</code>.</p>\n<h4>Example</h4><p>Table <code>daily_stock</code>:</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>sku</th><th>day</th><th>qty</th></tr><tr><td>A</td><td>2026-03-01</td><td>5</td></tr><tr><td>A</td><td>2026-03-02</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><td>A</td><td>2026-03-03</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><td>A</td><td>2026-03-04</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><td>A</td><td>2026-03-05</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>A</td><td>2026-03-06</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><td>B</td><td>2026-03-03</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><td>B</td><td>2026-03-05</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><td>C</td><td>2026-03-01</td><td>4</td></tr></table></div><p>the output should be</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>sku</th><th>streak_start</th><th>streak_end</th><th>days</th></tr><tr><td>A</td><td>2026-03-02</td><td>2026-03-04</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>B</td><td>2026-03-03</td><td>2026-03-03</td><td>1</td></tr></table></div>\n<p>For <code>B</code>, the stockout days of 3 and 5 March are not consecutive, because 4 March is missing, so its longest streaks have <code>1</code> day and the earliest is kept.</p><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 10 seconds (psql)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 1 GB</div>","starter":"/* Write your PostgreSQL query here */\n","hints":[],"summary_fr":"","tags":["gaps and islands","ROW_NUMBER","dates","PARTITION BY"],"minutes":20,"source":"Kata Lab","files":null,"visible":[{"input":{"tables":{"daily_stock":{"columns":[["sku","TEXT"],["day","DATE"],["qty","INT"]],"rows":[["A","2026-03-01",5],["A","2026-03-02",0],["A","2026-03-03",0],["A","2026-03-04",0],["A","2026-03-05",2],["A","2026-03-06",0],["B","2026-03-03",0],["B","2026-03-05",0],["C","2026-03-01",4]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["sku","streak_start","streak_end","days"],"rows":[["A","2026-03-02","2026-03-04",3],["B","2026-03-03","2026-03-03",1]]}},{"input":{"tables":{"daily_stock":{"columns":[["sku","TEXT"],["day","DATE"],["qty","INT"]],"rows":[["X","2026-02-27",0],["X","2026-02-28",0],["X","2026-03-01",0],["X","2026-03-02",null],["X","2026-03-03",0],["Y","2026-03-10",0],["Y","2026-03-11",0],["Y","2026-03-12",0]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["sku","streak_start","streak_end","days"],"rows":[["X","2026-02-27","2026-03-01",3],["Y","2026-03-10","2026-03-12",3]]}}],"hidden_n":7,"hidden":"","solution":""}